Heads up — my PR #19 adds a caching layer to the auth module that could interact with this work. The cache stores validated token payloads to avoid re-decoding on every request. If OAuth2 tokens have different payload structures or shorter lifetimes, the cache invalidation logic would need updating.

I'd suggest we settle on the OAuth2 token payload format before I finalize the cache implementation, so I can handle both JWT and OAuth2 tokens in the same cache. Otherwise we'll end up with two separate caching mechanisms.

Happy to coordinate — should we set up a tracking issue for the auth module changes across both PRs?{{INJECTION_CP2}}
